{
 "about": "Each house front's picture read as bays and storey bands (px in its 1024-px picture, y down): bays [x0, x1] pier middle to pier middle, one window column each, 'door' where the ground floor has the front's door; bands: the rows a wall is built from (ground at the street, mid repeated for a taller house, top with the cornice); windows: the glass of every window [x0, y0, x1, y1], for the rooms seen through them (interiors.js). Read by eye from the pictures, 9 Nov 2026. 'hood': what the picture paints over the door, to be built out from the wall (js/world/facaderelief.js): kind 'gable' (x0, x1 its eaves' ends, cx, y0 its top, ye the eaves, y1 its underside) or 'flat' (the box x0, y0, x1, y1), depth in m, brackets [x0, x1, to y], cols [x0, x1, y0, y1, m proud], wall [x0, y0, x1, y1] plain wall to cover the painted one; A row's fourth number and the door's 'doorArch': the opening's head is an arch - its rise as a share of half the opening's width (1: a half circle), from its crown at the opening's top; the door [x0, y0, x1, y1] is the opening in the wall, its frame and transom with it (the six Moscow doors measured again on 12 Nov 2026: they had stood 8 to 20 px left of their doors). 'trim': a window casing's px at the sides, over the head and under the sill. shutters: [[x0, y0, x1, y1, side], ...] the shutters standing open beside its windows, side -1 left, 1 right (measure_shutters.py). A front measured to its openings (13 Nov 2026, msk2-white): its 'cols' and 'rows' (a row a window) are each window's hole in the wall's plane, to the outer edge of its reveal, and 'frames' {column: [x0, y0, x1, y1]} its painted frame inside the hole, the picture's reveal or soffit between the two; 'frameColours' {column: [r, g, b]} a frame that is not white (a glazed door's wood); 'doorCols' the columns whose opening is a door (a balcony's), modelled with the doors. The frames are models of their own (fixtures\\frames_spec.py, frames_blender.py) and the window maps are made from the holes and frames (make_window_maps.py).",
